description:
pkix-revocation/src/crl.rs line 174, inside CrlChecker::with_delta:

    let delta_base_num = base_crl_number(&delta_crl)
        .expect("deltaCRLIndicator OID confirmed present by has_delta_crl_indicator")
        .map_err(Error::CrlParseError)?;

This .expect() is in production (non-test) code. The invariant is logically sound — has_delta_crl_indicator is checked two lines above, and base_crl_number returns None only when the extension is absent. However:

1. Any future refactor that breaks the invariant will panic in production rather than return Err.
2. The convention for production Rust paths is to use .ok_or_else(|| ...) or .unwrap_or_else to convert Option to a proper Error — not expect().

The fix is:

    let delta_base_num = base_crl_number(&delta_crl)
        .ok_or(Error::DeltaCrlBaseMismatch)?  // should not happen but safe fallback
        .map_err(Error::CrlParseError)?;

This converts the unreachable None case to a recoverable error instead of a panic.

Category: R2 (.expect() in non-test production code)
